Execution time is dominated by FLOPS.

Possible tweak: exploit symmetric kernels
e.g., save line from conv1d() for later use.
Avoids nsamps multiplies for each re-use,
but requires some fearsome bookkeeping.

Should try this first INSIDE conv1d
(exploit horizontal symmetry)

Massive space-for-speed tweak:
separate line buffers for each UNIQUE COEFFICIENT.
(this is probably a loss....)
